        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 284.72,
          "end": 285.38,
          "en": "number.",
          "zh": "數字。"
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 285.38,
          "end": 288.23,
          "en": "So that's the shorter form of doing that conversion",
          "zh": "所以那是做那個轉換的較短形式"
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 288.23,
          "end": 293.81,
          "en": "and it's up to you whether you prefer the plus or parseInt, parseInt and parseFloat is of course more",
          "zh": "而由你決定你偏好加號或 parseInt，parseInt 和 parseFloat 當然更"
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 293.81,
          "end": 295.84000000000003,
          "en": "explicit about what it's doing,",
          "zh": "明確關於它在做什麼，"
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 295.85,
          "end": 298.19,
          "en": "the plus here is easy to overlook",
          "zh": "這裡的加號很容易被忽略"
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 298.19,
          "end": 303.48,
          "en": "and if you know I want to have a non-decimal number or I absolutely need a decimal place,",
          "zh": "而如果你知道我想要沒有小數的數字，或我絕對需要小數位，"
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 303.62,
          "end": 309.64,
          "en": "well then parseInt gives you that extra control, the plus will just give you the best fitting number.",
          "zh": "嗯，那麼 parseInt 給你那個額外控制，加號只會給你最合適的數字。"
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 309.64,
          "end": 314.96,
          "en": "So if it's a number without decimal places, it will keep that, if it's a number with decimal places, it",
          "zh": "所以如果它是沒有小數位的數字，它會保留那個，如果它是有小數位的數字，它"
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 314.96,
          "end": 317.82,
          "en": "will keep that as well. So parseInt and parseFloat",
          "zh": "也會保留那個。所以 parseInt 和 parseFloat"
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 317.84,
          "end": 322.77,
          "en": "also allows you to be more specific about which kind of number you want.",
          "zh": "也允許你更具體關於你想要哪種數字。"
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 322.85,
          "end": 328.64,
          "en": "Now if you ever would want to convert a number to a string, you could do this as well by adding dot to",
          "zh": "現在如果你曾經想把數字轉成字串，你也可以藉由加上 .to"
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 328.73,
          "end": 329.54,
          "en": "string.",
          "zh": "String 來做這個。"
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 329.63,
          "end": 331.55,
          "en": "That's another built-in function",
          "zh": "那是另一個內建函式"
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 331.55,
          "end": 335.75,
          "en": "tied to the number here which converts this number to a string.",
          "zh": "綁在這裡的數字上，它把這個數字轉成字串。"
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 335.75,
          "end": 342.77,
          "en": "This however is definitely used to in less cases I'd say because more often, you need to convert a string",
          "zh": "不過這個我會說絕對在較少情況被使用，因為更常，你需要把字串"
